{
 "total": 31.96,
 "planned": false,
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "These orcas make waves to knock seals off the ice.",
   "visual": "hook",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.957
  },
  {
   "text": "In Antarctica, seals rest on floating ice, where orcas can't reach them.",
   "visual": "floes",
   "start": 2.957,
   "end": 6.994
  },
  {
   "text": "One orca pokes its head up to look.",
   "visual": "spyhop",
   "start": 6.994,
   "end": 8.794
  },
  {
   "text": "It's called spy-hopping.",
   "visual": "spyhop",
   "start": 8.794,
   "end": 10.174
  },
  {
   "text": "When it spots a seal, they line up side by side.",
   "visual": "lineup",
   "start": 10.174,
   "end": 12.849
  },
  {
   "text": "They swim at the ice together.",
   "visual": "charge",
   "start": 12.849,
   "end": 14.336
  },
  {
   "text": "Their bodies push a big wave over it.",
   "visual": "wave",
   "start": 14.336,
   "end": 16.261
  },
  {
   "text": "It often takes a few waves.",
   "visual": "waves",
   "start": 16.261,
   "end": 18.032
  },
  {
   "text": "If the ice breaks, the next wave is even easier.",
   "visual": "breaks",
   "start": 18.032,
   "end": 20.758
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the weird part.",
   "visual": "weird",
   "start": 20.758,
   "end": 22.161
  },
  {
   "text": "They almost always pick the Weddell seal.",
   "visual": "weddell",
   "start": 22.161,
   "end": 24.598
  },
  {
   "text": "Even though most seals there are another kind.",
   "visual": "others",
   "start": 24.598,
   "end": 27.231
  },
  {
   "text": "Scientists still don't know why.",
   "visual": "mystery",
   "start": 27.231,
   "end": 28.978
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow BioNiche for more weird animals.",
   "visual": "cta",
   "start": 28.978,
   "end": 31.96
  }
 ],
